The body.touch rules at end override the landscape media query. We can reorder: move body.touch rules before the responsive media queries, or add a final landscape media query with body.touch overrides. Also for portrait small screens, body.touch weapon-hud bottom 215 overrides max-width 520 bottom 209 slightly (6px) - okay but should be consistent. Body.touch vehicle-hud bottom 258 overrides 252, fine. Radar top 97 overrides 91/98, fine. Prompt 205 overrides 198. The end rules seem intended for touch, but conflict with landscape.

Better solution: move `body.touch` rules above the media queries, so media queries can override with same specificity? `.weapon-hud` specificity 0,1,0 vs `body.touch .weapon-hud` 0,2,1, so media still loses regardless of order. Need media rules with `body.touch` specificity. So add at end:

